{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.DegreeOneBraidTrivialVolume","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.DegreeOneBraidTrivialVolume","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Span.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.no_linear_vol_of_span_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.no_linear_vol_of_span_top","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/degree-one-braid-trivial-volume.lean#L51-L59","doc":"**No linear volume.**  If `S` spans `M`, a linear functional that\nvanishes on `S` cannot take a nonzero value anywhere.  This is the\ncontrapositive form used in the narrative: since the figure-eight\nelement has nonzero volume, `Vol` is not linear on `H_3(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Photon.linearVol_eq_zero_of_mem_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Photon.linearVol_eq_zero_of_mem_span","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/degree-one-braid-trivial-volume.lean#L36-L49","doc":"**A linear functional vanishing on a set vanishes on its span.**\n\nApplied with `M = H_n(q)`, `S` the positive permutation braids and\n`vol` any linear candidate for the hyperbolic volume, this shows the\ncandidate is identically zero on `H_n(q)`; it therefore cannot equal\n`Vol` on a hyperbolic closure such as `4₁`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:degree-one-braid-trivial-volume","label":"lem:degree-one-braid-trivial-volume","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/degree-one-braid-trivial-volume.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}